cff-version: "1.2.0"
type: software

title: "Toy GPT: Attention-Based Next-Token Model trained on Analytics Corpus"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-02"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/toy-gpt/train-600-attention"
url: "https://toy-gpt.github.io/train-600-attention/"
license: MIT

abstract: >
  A minimal, inspectable next-token prediction model using a single-head
  self-attention mechanism trained on a technical analytics micro-lessons
  corpus. Introduces dynamic context weighting: rather than treating all
  context tokens equally (as in the embeddings model), attention learns
  which prior tokens matter most for each prediction. Implements scaled
  dot-product attention from scratch in pure Python without deep learning
  frameworks. Part of the Toy GPT educational series; the final step in
  the progression from unigram frequency tables to attention-based
  neural language models.

